@startuml
title Order one-time transfer (with optional currency conversion)
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow false
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
actor "Customer" as customer
participant "Customer Web App\n(React SPA)" as spa
participant "Core Banking API\n(FastAPI)" as api
database "PostgreSQL" as db

customer -> spa : Fills in the New Transfer form: source account, recipient IBAN, amount, currency, description
opt currency differs from the source account currency (conversion preview)
spa -> api : GET /exchange-rates/latest?base=EUR&target=PLN
api -> db : SELECT rate FROM exchange_rates WHERE base/target match ORDER BY rate_timestamp DESC LIMIT 1
db --> api : rate, rate_timestamp
api --> spa : current rate
spa --> customer : Shows Currency Conversion box: current rate and estimated total charge
end
customer -> spa : Clicks Make a Transfer
spa -> api : POST /transfers {sourceAccountId, recipientAccountNumber, amount, currency, description}
api -> api : Authenticates the user (token) and validates the payload (amount > 0, IBAN format)
api -> db : BEGIN; SELECT ... FROM accounts WHERE id = :source OR account_number = :recipient ORDER BY id FOR UPDATE
db --> api : both account rows locked
alt source not owned by user / account not ACTIVE / recipient not found
api -> db : ROLLBACK
api --> spa : 403 / 404 / 422 error
spa --> customer : Shows error message
else accounts are valid
opt currencies differ (Convert currency)
api -> api : Converts: converted amount = amount x latest rate (Decimal, 4 decimal places)
note over api
Ledger must balance per currency, so a conversion is booked as 4 entries via the INTERNAL account (design proposal)
end note
end
api -> db : INSERT INTO transactions (reference_number, description, status = POSTED)
api -> db : INSERT INTO ledger: DEBIT on source account, CREDIT on recipient account
note over db
Triggers: ledger_apply_to_balance updates balances, chk_balance rejects balance < 0, trg_ledger_balanced checks DEBIT = CREDIT at COMMIT
end note
alt insufficient funds (chk_balance violated)
db --> api : error: check_violation
api -> db : ROLLBACK
api --> spa : 422 Insufficient funds
spa --> customer : Shows 'insufficient funds'
else success
api -> db : COMMIT
db --> api : committed
api --> spa : 201 Created {transactionId, referenceNumber, newBalance}
spa --> customer : Shows confirmation and the updated balance
end
end
@enduml
